ke Kate Moss and Naomi Campbell who walked for free, responding to wolf howls in the soundtrack. Invitations were tea-stained scrolls, leading guests to a stark Louvre runway that starkly contrasted with the opulent, modified ball gowns, panniers, and micro kilts. This decadent, fairytale-inspired presentation, a testament to Galliano's \"enfant terrible\" brilliance, captivated fashion elites including Anna Wintour. Its success, earning him British Designer of the Year, directly propelled him to become the first British designer to lead Givenchy in 1995, solidifying his place in fashion history.","shortHeadline":"Galliano Fashion Collection","topic":"Fashion","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/52270-6a761d8ee99f86bc035ead2c"}],"audioUrl":"https://cdn.jwplayer.com/videos/LmgvmiVO-3GQxW5ax.m4a","mediaId":"LmgvmiVO","audioDurationS":291,"audioFormat":"audio/mp4","generatedAt":"2026-08-08T08:30:40-05:00"},{"id":"BRIEF-2026-08-07-MORNING","cadence":"morning","date":"2026-08-07","script":"You're listening to The Daily Brief, your essential news update from Forbes. It's Friday, August 7. Today, we're highlighting the key stories covering Defense, US Politics, and a closer look at Political Campaigns.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nLeading off with, Iran war has reportedly depleted crucial weapons stockpiles—which trump denies. Sara Dorn has been tracking this development and reports that\n\nPresident Donald Trump vehemently denied a U.S. munitions shortage on Thursday, threatening \"long term jail sentences\" for \"leakers\" spreading what he called \"treasonous statements\" on Truth Social. He asserted the U.S. possesses \"massive amounts\" of munitions, with large quantities being manufactured. This denial follows multiple reports, including one from Reuters, claiming the U.S. Army has depleted \"virtually all\" its global long-range precision missile stockpile, impacting both U.S. and allied operations. The alleged shortage reportedly forces Trump to consider riskier piloted aircraft for attacks. The Washington Post also reported Trump accused Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth of misleading him about missile and interceptor shortages during a Camp David meeting, with Hegseth reportedly blaming his deputy. However, White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt dismissed these reports as \"100% fake news,\" while a Pentagon spokesperson called claims of depleted stockpiles and internal disagreements \"fictional.\" Beyond long-range missiles, reports indicate significant depletion of Tomahawk cruise missiles and ballistic missile interceptors. These developments unfold as Trump has recently walked back threats against Iran, with a potential deal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz now emerging.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nRead the full report on that story at Forbes.com. Moving now to, McConnell discharged from rehab—just before senate’s 5-week recess, a story that's currently shaping the landscape in US Politics.\n\nSenator Mitch McConnell, R-Ky., announced Thursday his discharge from a rehabilitation center following a June fall. He will continue intensive physical therapy at home during the Senate's five-week recess, while still engaging with staff on Senate business. This is his third health update since the June 14 fall, which left him briefly unconscious, prompting transparency calls. His initial June 13 statement, with wife Elaine Chao, confirmed hospitalization for mild pneumonia, ruling out broken bones, concussion, or severe issues. A July 28 update, also with a photo, noted his rehab transfer, where he remained medically uncleared, missing a Kentucky event and a colleague's funeral. His doctor previously cited childhood polio as a significant factor in his mobility. McConnell's absence has complicated the Senate's legislative calendar, given the Republicans' slim 53-47 majority. Without him, the Senate Appropriations Committee is split 14-14, effectively halting legislation without bipartisan support.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nTo finish today's update, we're turning to, Max miller accuses bernie moreno of ‘lies’ about daughter’s stuffed bunny. This headline is generating significant interest within Political Campaigns.\n\nSenator Bernie Moreno, R-Ohio, publicly lambasted Representative Max Miller, R-Ohio, on Tuesday, detailing a contentious custody exchange where Miller allegedly refused to return Moreno's granddaughter's beloved \"little blue bunny.\" Moreno described the incident as an act of \"total and complete depravity,\" stating Miller \"held it hostage for 48 hours,\" causing the two-year-old significant distress. The custody transfer, which Moreno handled at a suburban Cleveland police station due to fears about Miller's behavior, underscores the ongoing, heated dispute between Moreno's daughter and Miller. Moreno reiterated his call for Miller's resignation, asserting that Miller \"fails to meet that minimum basic standard\" for public office and that his daughter \"lives in constant fear of this man.\" This public escalation follows Miller's recent video statement denying abuse allegations from Moreno's daughter. Further developments Tuesday included Miller's attorney accepting responsibility for publishing an unclothed photo of their daughter in documents Miller released to support his innocence claims. Additionally, the House Ethics Committee announced an investigation into Miller, a probe he had requested himself to clear his name amidst the allegations.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nThat wraps up this edition of The Daily Brief. Be sure to check back tomorrow for our next update. Thanks for listening.","scriptTemplateId":1,"articles":[{"title":"Iran War Has Reportedly Depleted Crucial Weapons Stockpiles—Which Trump Denies","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2026/08/06/iran-war-has-reportedly-depleted-crucial-weapons-stockpiles-which-trump-denies/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a74b877f8a09394c