over abortion rights. Durkee previously covered U.S. politics at Vanity Fair and Mic, and as a theatre journalist she served as a New York Outer Critics Circle voter. Forbes reporters follow company ethical guidelines that ensure the highest quality. Follow her for continued coverage of Trump’s ongoing legal issues, the 2024 election and major cases at the Supreme Court.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/601b719e57b3eb66edb9e4a3/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1080\u0026cropY1=0\u0026cropY2=1080","authorSlug":"alisondurkee","authorType":"Forbes Staff","summary":"President Donald Trump’s $10 billion lawsuit against the BBC could unintentionally force him to shed light on his own personal finances, as the trust holding the president’s assets was ordered Monday to turn over financial documents to the broadcaster in order to prove Trump’s business and reputation was damaged as much as he claims.","shortHeadline":"Trump's Financial Records","topic":"Legal Affairs","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/50564-6a68dbb106a0475f11d0ad40"}],"audioUrl":"https://cdn.jwplayer.com/videos/Ujtwdpue-3GQxW5ax.m4a","mediaId":"Ujtwdpue","audioDurationS":208,"audioFormat":"audio/mp4","generatedAt":"2026-07-29T06:30:36-05:00"},{"id":"BRIEF-2026-07-28-MORNING","cadence":"morning","date":"2026-07-28","script":"Welcome to The Daily Brief, a look at today's top reporting from Forbes. It's Tuesday, July 28. On the agenda today: the latest developments in Politics, Politics, and Luxury Travel.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nDiving into the Politics space, we start with, McConnell ‘not yet medically cleared’ for senate return—kentucky gov. demands more details. According to reporting from Sara Dorn\n\nSenator Mitch McConnell remains in a rehabilitation facility, not yet medically cleared to leave over six weeks after a fall and subsequent bout of pneumonia. His office released a new statement confirming his continued recovery, indicating he will miss the upcoming Fancy Farm Picnic and likely Senator Lindsey Graham's funeral. McConnell's attending physician detailed that he is undergoing a \"strenuous course of physical therapy and rehabilitation\" aimed at rebuilding strength and mitigating future fall risks. The physician also highlighted that McConnell's childhood polio significantly impacts his mobility. A new photo of McConnell with his wife, Transportation Secretary Elaine Chao, was shared, following an earlier release two weeks prior that addressed growing speculation about his prolonged absence from the Senate. Despite his ongoing recovery, a spokesperson confirmed that McConnell continues to meet with staff to discuss Senate and Kentucky business. The 84-year-old, who is set to retire this year, has faced numerous health challenges, including two serious falls in 2023 and 2024. He also experienced two public freezing episodes in 2023, which his office attributed to lightheadedness, though some neurologists suggested mini-seizures. He often requires assistance with mobility.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nFor more context on that story, visit Forbes.com. Next, we shift our focus to, Trump says relationship with thune is ‘fine’ after demanding he cancel congressional vacation, a story that could have significant implications for Politics.\n\nFormer President Donald Trump has issued a direct rebuke to Senate Majority Leader John Thune, demanding the Senate not break for its August recess until the \"Save America Act\" is passed. Trump, in a Truth Social post, criticized Thune's leadership, stating Democrats were \"lucky\" with him and that \"stupidity always brings LOSING \u0026 DEATH!\" The \"Save America Act,\" which mandates documentary proof of citizenship for voter registration, remains stalled in the Senate. Its passage requires overcoming the 60-vote filibuster threshold, necessitating unlikely Democratic support. Even eliminating the filibuster itself would require 60 votes. White House Press Secretary Karoline Leavitt echoed Trump's sentiment, indicating his \"patience is running out\" with Thune and emphasizing the desire for the Act's passage before the recess, scheduled from August 7 to September 14. Senator Mike Lee has also advocated for a roll call vote to cancel the recess until the bill advances. Thune, however, pushed back, suggesting the White House should focus on convincing Democrats or even Republican senators like Susan Collins and Lisa Murkowski, who have opposed the bill, rather than blaming Republican leadership.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nOur final story today looks at, The most expensive lake weekends in canada aren’t in muskoka, new analysis finds. This remains a major point of conversation in the world of Luxury Travel.\n\nA new study by Casinos Analyzer Canada reveals that a two-night cottage getaway in some of Canada's top lake destinations can be surprisingly costly, with Atlantic Canada now leading in expense. The analysis, which factored in cottage rentals, fuel, groceries, drinks, and firewood, found Nova Scotia to be the most expensive, averaging $1,347. This is largely due to accommodation costs exceeding $1,000 for two nights and high alcohol prices. Ontario's renowned Muskoka region, often perceived as the priciest, came in a close second at $1,308, with rentals around $974. British Columbia's Okanagan ranked third at $1,259, notable for its high fuel expenses despite slightly lower accommodation. Kawartha Lakes, Ontario, followed at $1,235, benefiting from shorter drives from Toronto. Quebec's Laurentians offered a more budget-friendly option at $1,192, partly due to cheaper groceries and alcohol, securing the fifth spot among the surveyed regions. Canadians planning summer lake escapes should budget accordingly, as costs vary significantly across the country.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou're all caught up with The Daily Brief. Join us again tomorrow for your next news digest. Thanks for joining us.","scriptTemplateId":2,"articles":[{"title":"McConnell ‘Not Yet Medically Cleared’ For Senate Return—Kentucky Gov. Demands More Details","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2026/07/27/mitch-mcconnell-not-yet-medically-cleared-for-senate-return-new-statement-says/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a6782e8531446b51e884450/960x0.jpg","author":"Sara Dorn","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/5010031","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn","authorBio":"Sara Dorn is a Forbes news reporter who covers politics, with a focus on elections and Capitol Hill. She joined Forbes in 2022 and is based in New York. She's covered the 2022 midterms, 2024 presidential campaign, the January 6 House committee investigation, former House Speaker Kevin McCarthy's historic ouster, the 2023 State of the Union Address, former President Donald Trump's federal election interference and classified documents cases and his Manhattan hush money case. Dorn graduated in 2012 from the University of Dayton with a degree in journalism. Prior to joining Forbes, she covered New York City and state politics for the New York Post and City and State magazine. Follow her for updates and analysis on the 2024 presidential race, key Senate and House races and developments in Congress and at the White House.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/63457b718c2404f82daa3149/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1284\u0026cropY1=403\u0026cropY2=1687","authorSlug":"saradorn","authorType":"Forbes Staff","summary":"Senator Mitch McConnell remains in a rehabilitation facility, not yet medically cleared to leave over six weeks after a fall and subsequent bout of pneumonia. His office released a new statement confirming his continued recovery, indicating he will miss the upcoming Fancy Farm Picnic and likely Senator Lindsey Graham's funeral. McConnell's attending physician detailed that he is undergoing a \"strenuous course of physical therapy and reh