flecting pool is not apparent in latest photos. Sara Dorn has been following this story and reports that\n\nPresident Donald Trump has significantly escalated his claims regarding alleged vandalism at the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool, now asserting \"vandals\" caused 300-yard slashes in the liner. This follows earlier claims of gashes ranging from 250 to 350 feet. The pool was recently drained again, purportedly to repair this damage. However, photographic and video evidence of the empty basin does not support Trump's assertion of extensive gashes. Instead, some visible parallel markings have led to speculation they might be from Trump's motorcade, which drove over the liner in May. Previous images also showed the new blue surface peeling, though not necessarily due to cutting. Trump had previously described the liner as \"very strong\" and un-cuttable, clarifying it's a \"high grade colored waterproofing liner.\" The Trump administration has yet to produce evidence for the vandalism claims, which also include allegations of fertilizer being dumped to cause algae. At least seven individuals have been arrested in connection with alleged vandalism, including former Olympian David Hearn, who denies forcefully damaging the liner, stating he only touched a detached piece. The controversial renovation project's cost has soared from an initial $1.8 million to over $15 million.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou can find the full analysis of that story at Forbes.com. Now, we're turning our attention to, Trump’s intel nominee jay clayton won’t say biden won, but insists he’s ‘not an election denier’, a development that could have a lasting impact on Politics.\n\nPresident Donald Trump’s nominee for director of national intelligence, Jay Clayton, notably refused to affirm who won the 2020 election during his confirmation hearing. Despite being pressed by Democratic senators, Clayton evaded direct answers, stating, \"I’m not going to do this with you.\" When asked by Sen. Mark Warner if he denied Joe Biden won, Clayton insisted he is \"not an election denier\" and acknowledged Biden was \"certified as the president.\" However, he also emphasized the need for \"substantial work to do in improving our electoral processes,\" aligning with Trump's ongoing narrative. Sen. Jon Ossoff sharply criticized Clayton, asking if it wasn't \"humiliating to be unable to answer this question\" and to \"indulge the president’s delusions.\" This contentious exchange occurred as Trump prepares to deliver a prime-time speech Thursday, teasing \"really, really big news\" concerning \"free and fair elections.\" Democrats, including Warner and Ossoff, expressed alarm, fearing Trump's speech aims to mislead Americans and lay groundwork for election interference. Clayton, a former SEC chair, was nominated by Trump to replace Tulsi Gabbard, who was also involved in the administration's 2020 election probes.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nRounding out today's briefing, we look at, The world’s best gin, according to the global spirits masters. This story is currently at the center of the conversation in Spirits.\n\nThe Global Spirits Masters competition recently honored seven exceptional gins with its top Master designation. Judged purely on quality by an international panel, these award-winners showcase remarkable global diversity and craftsmanship. Stauning Danish Dry Gin impressed with its Nordic botanicals and grain-focused expertise, offering a fresh, juniper-forward profile. Mayfair London Dry Gin exemplified classic balance and traditional character, while Tanqueray No. TEN, a luxury pioneer, stood out for its vibrant fresh citrus and benchmark London Dry style. From Iceland, Marberg Dry Gin utilized pure glacial water and native Arctic botanicals, reflecting its pristine origins. Slovenia's Gin Burje presented a distinctive regional identity through local herbs. AmberChes Botanical Gin achieved harmony with a broad spectrum of floral and spicy notes, thanks to precision distillation. Finally, Norway's LØV Nordic Gin celebrated Scandinavian forests with local spruce tips and wild berries. These selections collectively affirm that world-class gin production now spans far beyond traditional regions, highlighting the industry's dynamic creativity and evolving botanical landscapes.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou've reached the end of this Daily Brief. Tune in again for tomorrow's updates. Thanks for joining us.","scriptTemplateId":0,"articles":[{"title":"Huge Gash Trump Claims ‘Vandals’ Made In Reflecting Pool Is Not Apparent In Latest Photos","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2026/07/15/huge-gash-trump-claims-vandals-made-in-reflecting-pool-is-not-apparent-in-latest-photos/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a57a0707f34fd87173d9cfd/960x0.jpg","author":"Sara Dorn","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/5010031","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn","authorBio":"Sara Dorn is a Forbes news reporter who covers politics, with a focus on elections and Capitol Hill. She joined Forbes in 2022 and is based in New York. She's covered the 2022 midterms, 2024 presidential campaign, the January 6 House committee investigation, former House Speaker Kevin McCarthy's historic ouster, the 2023 State of the Union Address, former President Donald Trump's federal election interference and classified documents cases and his Manhattan hush money case. Dorn graduated in 2012 from the University of Dayton with a degree in journalism. Prior to joining Forbes, she covered New York City and state politics for the New York Post and City and State magazine. Follow her for updates and analysis on the 2024 presidential race, key Senate and House races and developments in Congress and at the White House.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/63457b718c2404f82daa3149/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1284\u0026cropY1=403\u0026cropY2=1687","authorSlug":"saradorn","authorType":"Forbes Staff","summary":"President Donald Trump has significantly escalated his claims regarding alleged vandalism at the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool, now asserting \"vandals\" caused 300-yard slashes in the liner. This follows earlier claims of gashes ranging from 250 to 350 feet. The pool was recently drained again, purportedly to repair this damage. However, photographic and video evidence of the empty basin does not support Trump's assertion of extensive gashes. Instead, some visible parallel markings have led to speculation they might be from Trump's motorcade, which drove over the liner in May. Previous images also showed the new blue surface peeling, though not necessarily due to cutting. Trump had previously described the liner as \"very strong\" and un-cuttable, clarifying it's a \"high grade colored waterproofing liner.\" The Trump administration has yet to produce evidence for the vandalism claims, which also include allegations of fertilizer being dumped to cause algae. At least seven individuals have been arrested in connection with alleged vandalism, including former Olympian David Hearn, who denies forcefully damaging the liner, stating he only touched a detached piece. The controversial renovation project's cost has soared from an initial $1.8 million to over $15 million.","shortHeadline":"Reflecting Pool Damage","topic":"Trump News","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/51554-6a57a02798ab8998c78c63e4"},{"title":"Trump’s Intel Nominee Jay Clayton Won’t Say Biden Won, But Insists He’s ‘Not An Election Denier’","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2026/07/15/trumps-intel-nominee-jay-clayton-wont-say-biden-won-but-insists-hes-not-an-election-denier/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a57b35fa20c1c47dde1e057/960x0.jpg","author":"Sara Dorn","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/5010031","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn","authorBio":"Sara Dorn is a Forbes news repor